            <p>This allows for initial recovery, stitch removal, and follow-up consultations before traveling home.</p>

            <h3>Will I need someone to accompany me?</h3>
            <p>For major procedures under general anesthesia, yes. You will need a responsible adult to accompany you for at least the first 24-48 hours. If you don't have someone traveling with you, hospitals can arrange medical nurses or patient liaisons to assist during your recovery.</p>

            <h3>What happens if I need a revision?</h3>
            <p>Revision rates vary by procedure and surgeon experience (typically 5-10% for rhinoplasty, lower for other procedures). Discuss revision policies before booking:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Some surgeons include one revision in their fee within a certain timeframe</li>
                <li>You may need to travel back to China for revisions</li>
                <li>Budget for potential revision costs (usually significantly less than original surgery)</li>
                <li>Get everything in writing regarding revision policies</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>How do I verify a surgeon's credentials?</h3>
            <p>Ask the hospital for the surgeon's:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Medical license number (verifiable through Chinese Medical Association)</li>
                <li>Board certification documentation</li>
                <li>Number of years in practice</li>
                <li>Number of procedures performed annually</li>
                <li>Photos of previous patients with similar concerns</li>
                <li>Professional society memberships (ISAPS, Chinese Association of Plastic Surgery)</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Can I combine multiple procedures?</h3>
            <p>Yes, combination surgery is common and can be cost-effective. Popular combinations include:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Mommy Makeover: Tummy tuck + Breast surgery + Liposuction</li>
                <li>Facial rejuvenation: Facelift + Eyelid surgery + Brow lift</li>
                <li>Body contouring: Liposuction + Fat transfer to buttocks or breasts</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Your surgeon will advise on safe combinations based on procedure length and your health status. Combined procedures typically take 4-8 hours and require longer recovery.</p>

